2. It frees the original string after the first match, so it no longer has the full string to search.

3. The new length calculation only accounts for replacing the first match, not any subsequent matches.

To make it work for multiple matches, we would need to:

1. Continually reallocate a new, larger buffer as more matches are found 
2. Continue searching the original string for more matches 
3. Update the new length calculation after each match to account for all replacements so far

